WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.493 --> 00:00:19.495
This is Jugner Forest. Every tree or rock inside a region that is not cut out as a hole is ground where the server may try to spawn a mob. Cutting them one at a time is slow; the Carve holes tool finds them for you.

2
00:00:19.495 --> 00:00:26.102
Select the region, here east three-ten. Some of its trees have holes, several do not.

3
00:00:26.102 --> 00:00:37.503
The Spawns button shows it: green is where the server would put a mob, red a spot it throws away because it is off the walkable ground.

4
00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:47.709
Open Carve holes. Amber outlines are obstacles found in the zone's collision mesh; violet dashed ones are patches no mob was ever recorded on.

5
00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:51.919
Hover Ring all to preview everything it would cut.

6
00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:55.876
Click it, and each obstacle becomes a hole.

7
00:00:55.876 --> 00:01:05.677
Cut patches does the same for the empty ground. The clearance dial above it keeps each patch that far from where mobs walked.

8
00:01:05.677 --> 00:01:23.878
A cut that would split the region in two is left alone, and says so. Anything left dashed is too big for Ring all, usually a cliff or a hillside: click it on the map to cut it on its own, or leave it.

9
00:01:23.878 --> 00:01:32.477
Press Escape to leave the tool. The new holes are ordinary holes: drag, grow or delete them like any other.

10
00:01:32.478 --> 00:01:41.078
Every cut is one step in History, so Control Z takes back the last one if it went too far.
